# monitoring — runtime configuration template.
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. `make run` loads `.env` automatically.
# For the built binary:  set -a; . ./.env; set +a; ./bin/monitoring

# --- IAM Identity Center (SSO) — required ---
MONITORING_SSO_START_URL=
MONITORING_SSO_REGION=
AWS_ACCOUNT_ID=
MONITORING_SSO_ROLE=

# --- MaxMind GeoLite2 (per-IP country drill-down; auto-downloaded at startup) ---
# Free account + license key: https://www.maxmind.com/en/geolite2/signup
# Only the license key is needed (the download permalink authenticates by
# license_key; no account id). Leave blank to disable auto-download — the world
# view still works; the country drill-down just returns no points.
GEOIP_LICENSE_KEY=
# GEOIP_AUTO_UPDATE=true
# GEOIP_DB_PATH=./GeoLite2-City.mmdb

# --- Athena / Glue (defaults shown; uncomment to override) ---
# REGION=eu-central-1
# ATHENA_DATABASE=platform-monitoring
# ATHENA_WORKGROUP=platform-monitoring

# --- Log sources ---
# Auto-discovered at startup from the Glue catalog (the tables `terraform apply`
# created) using the credentials obtained at SSO login — nothing to set here.
# The catalog is the single source of truth (edit var.log_sources + apply to
# change it). Optionally override with an explicit JSON list (e.g. to query a
# subset, or for offline testing); when set, it wins over discovery:
# LOG_SOURCES='[{"name":"alexandria","table":"alexandria"}]'
